  "comments": "<p>2000P tail feathers<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/639c7b9b4a36c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/639c7b9b4a36c.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>The Sacagawea Dollar proved to be unpopular amongst the American public and are today rarely seen in everyday commerce. However, they are frequently used in Ecuador and El Salvador, two nations that have adopted the United States dollar.<br><br>The standard weight of all base-metal dollars issued since 2000 is 125 grains.<br>&nbsp;</p><p>2000 P Wounded eagle dollar link: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer ugc\" href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/coinfacts/coin/2000-p-sac-1-wounded-eagle/506153\">https://www.pcgs.com/coinfacts/coin/2000-p-sac-1-wounded-eagle/506153</a></p>",
